WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: zh

00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:01.599
I didn't draw today

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.900
I'm such a piece of garbage

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.733
I had a plan to draw

00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:05.966
But the delay went on and on

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:06.866
And the most shameful thing is

00:00:06.866 --> 00:00:09.799
I wasted all that time scrolling through my phone

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.499
Teacher, if I'm really hopeless

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.500
This is a question asked by a student

00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:16.199
Look at the way he's asking it

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.733
So I had the rest of the conversation with him

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:19.766
Which picture is it

00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:21.566
That's what makes you feel so frustrated

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.166
Can you send it to me

00:00:23.466 --> 00:00:25.766
Is there some technical difficulty in the painting

00:00:25.766 --> 00:00:26.599
Stuck you

00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:28.966
It may seem like a big problem to you

00:00:29.066 --> 00:00:30.733
Send it to me and discuss it with me

00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:32.466
It might not be that hard to deal with him

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:35.099
It also gives me a chance to study the difficulty of this technique

00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:35.866
Not these problem teachers

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:39.199
You've made yourself very clear

00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:41.866
I understand everything you've said

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.133
I literally didn't make a single move

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.133
Ming Ming also likes painting

00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:47.899
I really want to draw

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.266
But I'm so bad

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:52.066
I just can't help scrolling through my phone

00:00:52.466 --> 00:00:53.133
In general

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:55.766
A person to do a thing depends on motivation

00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:57.899
Resistance and consequences Three factors

00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:00.699
So far there doesn't seem to be any technical resistance

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:02.166
You said you liked drawing

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.266
That looks like a lot of power, too

00:01:04.466 --> 00:01:06.733
There may be consequences for you of not doing this

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.266
It doesn't really matter, right

00:01:08.766 --> 00:01:11.133
Maybe he's worried he can't do it right

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:13.866
I always feel like if I don't do something right

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:14.966
Might as well not do it

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.300
So there's always a lot of mental building going on

00:01:18.366 --> 00:01:20.666
And be ready to put yourself in a state

00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:23.133
Adjust to a point where it feels good

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.066
Then starting

00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:26.766
For example, if the light is bad today

00:01:26.966 --> 00:01:29.333
I thought it might not be a good idea

00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:31.666
And if I feel like I'm in a state of mind

00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:33.299
I don't really want to paint

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.166
I have a lot on my mind

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.000
I wouldn't have chosen to do it

00:01:37.466 --> 00:01:39.066
I don't seem to be in that state

00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:41.933
For me painting technique is one of the things I like

00:01:42.066 --> 00:01:43.166
It's my job

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:44.866
If I stop painting

00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:47.499
I would feel that there is a stagnation in technology and teaching

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:49.933
There is no way to appreciate more problems and progress

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.666
I lost my thinking about painting

00:01:51.766 --> 00:01:53.733
Then my job would be bad, too

00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:55.966
These are serious consequences for me

00:01:56.066 --> 00:01:57.099
So even today

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.466
I'm not necessarily going to draw anything that I'm happy with

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.566
Or not trying to do a good job

00:02:01.566 --> 00:02:02.866
I will insist on doing it

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.600
May have eased my anxiety to some extent

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.733
Maybe for you

00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:08.599
Being perfect has a special meaning

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.900
Imperfection is a serious consequence

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.200
He was one of the older ones that you started painting with

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.200
Psychological resistance

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:17.666
Yes, my parents were very strict with me growing up

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.666
Even though I got a 98

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:21.933
They will also ask me to reflect seriously

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:23.699
What's the problem with the two points

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.933
Sometimes he even abused and whipped me severely

00:02:26.933 --> 00:02:28.766
They hardly praised me

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.366
Later at work

00:02:30.366 --> 00:02:32.899
I met a similar leader

00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:33.966
He thinks highly of me

00:02:33.966 --> 00:02:35.599
But only my heart knows

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.800
I do a good job not because I like it

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.133
I just don't want to make a mistake

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.566
So I kind of like painting

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.333
Probably because I didn't sign up for classes before

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.799
And I rarely post my works on moments

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.700
So rarely do people ask me for anything

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.933
But as I paint for longer and longer

00:02:55.966 --> 00:02:58.333
The more you want to share your work

00:02:58.333 --> 00:02:59.266
At this time

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:02.299
A lot of inner voices began to ring

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.800
I keep warning myself

00:03:03.866 --> 00:03:06.099
Are you even allowed to draw like this

00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:07.733
Listen to your tone of voice

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.700
I don't sense any resentment towards your parents

00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:13.566
More is to hate their own iron into steel

00:03:13.966 --> 00:03:16.466
Looks like your parents might be the better ones

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.500
Not the kind of guy who just talks and doesn't walk

00:03:18.733 --> 00:03:21.099
I mean, it's very strict on you

00:03:21.166 --> 00:03:23.266
But it may also offer you a lot

00:03:23.266 --> 00:03:24.866
Practical advice and help

00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:27.399
You've grown a lot under their tutelage

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.700
Your guess is very accurate, Sir

00:03:29.866 --> 00:03:32.333
My parents are wonderful people

00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.199
They are the leaders of the system

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.400
respected

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.733
And it's not just me

00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:41.266
They are also strict with themselves and their subordinates

00:03:41.466 --> 00:03:44.266
When I meet with difficulties in study and work

00:03:44.366 --> 00:03:46.733
Will continue to teach me how to learn

00:03:46.766 --> 00:03:49.066
Told me to suffer from childhood

00:03:49.266 --> 00:03:52.933
In modern parlance, it is to keep doing things seriously

00:03:52.933 --> 00:03:54.733
To compound interest over time

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.266
To be the dragon of men

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.166
They have a regular schedule

00:03:58.166 --> 00:03:59.199
Little entertainment

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:02.200
My family are standard workaholics

00:04:02.266 --> 00:04:05.733
I couldn't even tell them I liked painting when I was a kid

00:04:05.866 --> 00:04:08.866
I did very well under their guidance

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.700
Always getting recognition at school and at work

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.100
But I do know

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.000
I'm really happy in painting

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:20.333
In fact, sometimes I procrastinate at work

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.966
We started right before the deadline

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.266
Although the end result is also OK

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:29.399
But I know I can do better

00:04:29.866 --> 00:04:32.599
I thought the delay was because I didn't like it

00:04:32.966 --> 00:04:36.999
But now I find in painting that I still procrastinate

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.966
I didn't expect that

00:04:39.066 --> 00:04:41.699
Why am I in something I love

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:42.866
Is it?

00:04:42.966 --> 00:04:45.299
What was supposed to take 100 hours

00:04:45.466 --> 00:04:47.533
It took the last 10 hours to finish

00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:48.899
It's not perfect

00:04:49.066 --> 00:04:50.333
But it's done

00:04:50.466 --> 00:04:52.699
Then the other 90 hours are all your own

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:53.866
High cost performance

00:04:53.966 --> 00:04:55.566
It's lazy and labor-saving

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.066
For the other 90 hours, I swiped my phone

00:04:58.066 --> 00:05:00.466
There's a lot of new information coming in

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.500
More happy!

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.200
We always feel like when we're on our phones

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.200
Not much to gain

00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:05.799
It's because of the time that we spent

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.166
It's not for harvest

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.666
It's exhausting to harvest

00:05:08.666 --> 00:05:10.066
It requires deep thinking

00:05:10.166 --> 00:05:11.699
It uses a lot of energy

00:05:11.866 --> 00:05:13.799
Procrastination combined with phone slamming

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:14.966
The brain is relaxed

00:05:15.066 --> 00:05:16.133
Saving energy consumption

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.733
It's what our brains are wired for

00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:20.733
We entered civilization only ten thousand years ago

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.300
Courage and millions of years of physical instinct

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.400
For us first is an animal

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.733
And then there's the individual

00:05:26.766 --> 00:05:28.166
That's full of reason

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.133
A man with ideals and passions

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.266
It's part of our many personalities

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.599
And we need to do it for our biological instincts once in a while

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.766
Part of the time

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.700
Eat and drink enough to brush the phone

00:05:38.866 --> 00:05:41.166
Even the occasional all-nighter won't hurt

00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:42.466
There's nothing wrong with that

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:45.166
The driver who controls the wheel in our body

00:05:45.166 --> 00:05:46.766
Not just the civilized man

00:05:46.766 --> 00:05:48.099
And an animal man

00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:50.399
Freud called him the id

00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:52.099
No matter how nasty he is

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.566
Vulgar lazy

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.000
That's us, too

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.500
We can't keep pressing him

00:05:56.566 --> 00:05:58.499
You gotta give him a chance to relax

00:05:58.566 --> 00:06:00.166
Otherwise, he would have quit the car

00:06:00.166 --> 00:06:01.699
You're slapping your brakes on the side

00:06:01.733 --> 00:06:02.999
Interfering with your steering wheel

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.399
Then you're in bad shape

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.900
We can't keep sniping at him

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.966
Get along with who you are

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.900
In fact, your inner self loves to procrastinate

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:12.266
That's very kind of you

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.600
Don't accuse him any more

00:06:13.866 --> 00:06:16.133
Maybe even give him a little more time

00:06:16.166 --> 00:06:17.166
Make it up to him.

00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:20.399
Teacher: This is the first time I've heard that

00:06:20.466 --> 00:06:21.766
I heard you say that

00:06:21.766 --> 00:06:24.099
I suddenly feel sorry for that me

00:06:24.366 --> 00:06:27.199
I even want to swipe my phone a little more now

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.600
But an elite man like my father

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.333
What's going on

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.733
Did their part of me get murdered by themselves

00:06:34.766 --> 00:06:37.766
Why else would they be able to work from morning till night

00:06:37.766 --> 00:06:39.566
What do you do for fun

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.533
Why didn't they make some changes

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:42.666
The state of things

00:06:42.966 --> 00:06:44.766
They've already done something sick

00:06:44.766 --> 00:06:46.099
You got a 98 on the test

00:06:46.166 --> 00:06:47.566
They're still doing it to you

00:06:47.566 --> 00:06:48.733
This is already sick

00:06:48.733 --> 00:06:50.066
Look at the barrage

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.533
One of my painting students

00:06:51.533 --> 00:06:51.733
In the

00:06:51.733 --> 00:06:54.533
A lot of it came from wanting to draw as a child

00:06:54.566 --> 00:06:55.666
Parents don't support

00:06:55.966 --> 00:06:57.899
You'll see it as we grow up

00:06:58.066 --> 00:06:59.499
Someone who's been pissed off out there

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.133
It's usually done at home

00:07:01.266 --> 00:07:02.799
Because of what is repressed

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.666
There has to be a place to release

00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:07.266
It's a shame that place is often home

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.966
Many of us want an apology from our parents

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.933
I've been begging my whole life

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:13.866
But it may never be

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.766
When you grow up

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.200
Maybe I can feel what they were going through

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.566
Different times, different lives

00:07:20.733 --> 00:07:23.599
But id drives life at a different price

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.933
We worked so hard

00:07:24.933 --> 00:07:26.133
Is to hope that the next generation

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:28.066
You can live a little wild

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:31.400
Teacher, what you said hit me

00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:34.766
I've been wanting to blame them for a while

00:07:34.866 --> 00:07:36.933
But once I understood them

00:07:36.966 --> 00:07:38.766
I don't think I can blame them

00:07:38.933 --> 00:07:40.933
There has always been a strange grievance

00:07:40.933 --> 00:07:42.899
There is no understanding or comfort

00:07:43.066 --> 00:07:44.666
I don't know who to go to

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.066
I didn't even talk to you today

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.533
I didn't even look at it

00:07:49.733 --> 00:07:51.766
I would have thought that was unreasonable

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.500
In a way

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.466
I've been very lucky

00:07:55.466 --> 00:07:57.733
My parents are strict

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.700
But they are not duplicitous domestic abusers

00:08:01.466 --> 00:08:03.099
Then he cried for some time

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:05.366
He said he felt better after he cried

00:08:05.566 --> 00:08:07.466
He said he would try it next

00:08:07.466 --> 00:08:08.599
Embrace that part

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.266
You want to swipe your phone

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.333
Later we were in a relatively relaxed context

00:08:12.333 --> 00:08:13.899
An interesting question

00:08:14.266 --> 00:08:16.299
There are always people in our lives

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.066
How often do you procrastinate

00:08:18.266 --> 00:08:19.899
What is the situation

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.333
Some experts say procrastination is addictive

00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:23.399
Because we found out

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.466
If it only takes a little time to get things done

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.966
Then it's cost-effective to put it off

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:30.799
But the expert only tells half the story

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.533
Because there's another group of people who know there are serious consequences

00:08:33.566 --> 00:08:35.099
But still he procrastinated

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.666
And it's really not done yet

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.366
The delay was overcome by intense pressure

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.866
Incapacitated

00:08:40.933 --> 00:08:42.699
Because they didn't think it would help

00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:45.366
Like the main force doing the job is too big

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.266
How to learn how to do will not give up

00:08:48.333 --> 00:08:49.066
And such as

00:08:49.066 --> 00:08:51.399
It feels like it doesn't really mean that much

00:08:51.466 --> 00:08:53.399
I've gone to so much trouble to get

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.900
It's really hard to beat

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:55.899
This kind of delay

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.000
Well, the main reason is that

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.700
I did something I didn't like

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.866
And being forced to do the hard stuff all the time

00:09:01.266 --> 00:09:03.533
Maybe this is the difficulty of being a man

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:06.100
We can't act like animals

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.100
Hungry to eat

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.300
Tired to sleep

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.800
Everything is done according to its own nature

00:09:10.933 --> 00:09:12.733
Because we're going to have to live

00:09:12.733 --> 00:09:15.466
Do all kinds of things that people tell you to do

00:09:15.766 --> 00:09:17.366
To accomplish other people's goals

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.766
You can't do what you love

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.666
The ones that make money don't

00:09:21.666 --> 00:09:23.099
Love does not make money

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.933
There was a time in my life when I secretly quit

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.966
Lived in the country for a while

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.599
I was surprised

00:09:30.733 --> 00:09:33.533
Vegetables and eggs are so cheap in the country

00:09:33.766 --> 00:09:36.566
Living expenses can be a few dollars a day

00:09:36.733 --> 00:09:39.566
I used to have trouble sleeping in the city

00:09:39.766 --> 00:09:42.099
Often stay up until 3 a.m

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:43.533
But when we get here

00:09:43.533 --> 00:09:46.499
I fell asleep before 10:00 naturally

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.733
It's quiet in the country at night

00:09:48.866 --> 00:09:51.466
Not a sound of traffic

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.200
Wake up naturally at four or five in the morning

00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:56.899
Pick a vegetable from the field and plant a field

00:09:57.066 --> 00:10:00.533
Go home and rest when the sun comes out

00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:03.266
Thoreau said it at Walden Pond

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.566
There's not much food to deliver to one person

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.200
And the technology now is really convenient

00:10:09.533 --> 00:10:12.199
You can relax all afternoon

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.300
Go for a walk in the evening when the sun is gone

00:10:15.366 --> 00:10:17.566
It's a very comfortable life

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.766
I sleep on a full stomach like the family cat

00:10:20.966 --> 00:10:24.799
Unfortunately, I start to get anxious over time

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.600
Although I have enough to lie down for years

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.566
But only in and out

00:10:29.566 --> 00:10:31.899
I see my savings getting smaller and smaller

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.133
I'm starting to lose my composure

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:37.466
I'll find myself rolling even when I'm lying flat

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.400
A variety of more comfortable reclining flats appeared

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:43.133
I realized I might be a loser at lying flat

00:10:43.333 --> 00:10:44.799
That's just my personality

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:46.700
There is no way to stop comparing

00:10:47.166 --> 00:10:49.899
Eventually I went back to work in the city

